---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout
  title="Organisation — LucrumTech"
  description="We build the organisation behind the business — structure, leadership, people and operating model — for companies being built and companies that have outgrown their structure."
>
  <section>
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">Organisation</p>
      <h1>Technology builds the product.<span class="muted">Organisation is what lets it keep running at scale.</span></h1>
      <p class="lede" style="margin-top:24px">We build the organisation behind the business — structure, leadership, people and operating model. For companies being built, and for companies that have outgrown the structure that once worked.</p>
      <div class="btnrow"><a class="btn" href="/contact">Book a conversation</a></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="tint">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">The argument</p>
      <h2>Not a bigger team. Not more process. The right system for the next stage.</h2>
      <p class="lede" style="margin-top:22px">A great product needs more than great technology. It needs the right leadership, the right capabilities, the right people, the right operating model.</p>
      <p class="lede">The work can start before there is an organisation, when there is only an idea. Or when a business has outgrown the structure that got it here. In both cases the objective is the same: build the right organisation for the business you are creating.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">From business model to organisation</p>
      <h2>The real question is rarely "who should we hire?"</h2>
      <p class="lede" style="margin-top:22px">It's: what organisation does this business need in order to work, grow and create value?</p>
      <p class="strong">Business model → capabilities → organisation → leadership → team → operating model → launch → scale</p>
      <div class="grid2">
        <div class="blk"><h3>Organisational strategy and design</h3><p>People strategy, organisational design, workforce planning, leadership architecture, performance management, culture.</p></div>
        <div class="blk"><h3>Business building and scaling</h3><p>Organisational architecture, team design, critical capabilities, leadership team, hiring strategy, in-house vs outsource, scaling model.</p></div>
        <div class="blk"><h3>Transformation and restructuring</h3><p>Organisational audit, redesign, operating model, roles and accountability, leadership transitions, team rebuild.</p></div>
        <div class="blk"><h3>Executive search and critical hiring</h3><p>C-level, VP and head-level roles — from search and assessment through selection, offer and 90-day integration.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="tint">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">Hiring</p>
      <h2>A placement that leaves in month three was never a placement.</h2>
      <p class="lede" style="margin-top:22px">Hiring runs on a defined process — intake through onboarding and probation follow-up, tracked in ATS with agreed response times at every stage. No black box, no candidate going quiet for three weeks.</p>
      <p class="lede">Most interviews test whether someone can do the job. We test three things: capability, fit with how the team actually works, and whether this is somewhere they will still want to be in two years. What the interview surfaces then shapes the onboarding — so the first 90 days are built around the specific person, not a template.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">Track record</p>
      <h2>15+ years. 350+ people built and scaled.</h2>
      <p class="lede" style="margin-top:22px">11+ years in technology. End-to-end organisational rebuilds delivered in three months. Across IT, outsourcing and outstaffing, technology products, FinTech, media, international businesses, corporations, holding structures and subsidiaries.</p>
      <div class="btnrow"><a class="btn" href="/contact">Book a conversation</a></div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
